        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Chacabuco</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">12 February 1817; one account puts the end of the fighting at 14:00</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hacienda">Hacienda</a> de Chacabuco in the valley of Chacabuco, Colina, about 55 km north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chile">Chile</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-the-andes">Army of the Andes</a>, of the United Provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a> and Chilean exiles, under Captain General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a> with Miguel Estanislao Soler and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardo-ohiggins">Bernardo O'Higgins</a>, in two columns of 2,000 and 1,500 men by one account; a royalist force under Brigadier Rafael Maroto of about 1,500 men, with up to 2,000 in another account</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The patriot army won. Royalist dead are given as 500 and prisoners as 600; patriot dead as 12. The patriots entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> within days and O'Higgins was named Supreme Director of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chile">Chile</a>.</span></div>
