    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>San Martín split his army into two columns to take the royalists from front and rear, but O'Higgins's column attacked before Soler's arrived, and accounts of what followed differ.</li><li>The royalists were fewer, about 1,500 men, and their governor had reversed the decision to retreat south the morning after it was taken, ordering Maroto to hold Chacabuco.</li><li>San Martín declined the post of governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chile">Chile</a> and an assembly of notable residents named O'Higgins Supreme Director, opening the period known as the Patria Nueva.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Black soldiers, mostly freed former slaves recruited in the interior provinces, are estimated at between 2,000 and 3,000 of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-the-andes">Army of the Andes</a>, and made up the majority of its 7th, 8th and 11th Infantry Regiments.</p></aside>
    </section>

